  "liner": {
   "body_md": "On October 3, 2023, the Mountain Goats performed at The Belasco in Los Angeles as part of their Spectral Tide tour [1][4]. This recording, captured by @lmgbtapes, is a matrix mix combining soundboard and audience microphones, documenting all twenty-two songs over 112 minutes [1]. It is the only archived recording of this specific performance, making it a valuable document of the night [1]. The setlist features a blend of material from albums such as Jenny from Thebes, Bleed Out, and Dark in Here, alongside rare tracks like “Guys on Every Corner” and “Cleaning Crew” [1][2]. Notably, the band performed “Only One Way,” which is the first appearance of that song in the archive, as well as “The Pig Song,” a bustout not heard in 1,628 days [2]. The show also included spoken introductions for “No Children” and banter referencing John Vanderslice [1]. This performance was the 386th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous show at Belly Up Tavern on October 2, 2023 [2]. The uploader thanked the venue crew and management for allowing the live taping [1]. A poster for the event was credited to UCLA Radio [7].",
